       In the glibc implementation, the mmqq__nnoottiiffyy() library function is
       implemented on top of the system call of the same name.  When _s_e_v_p is
       NULL, or specifies a notification mechanism other than SSIIGGEEVV__TTHHRREEAADD,
       the library function directly invokes the system call.  For
       SSIIGGEEVV__TTHHRREEAADD, much of the implementation resides within the library,
       rather than the kernel.  (This is necessarily so, since the thread
       involved in handling the notification is one that must be managed by
       the C library POSIX threads implementation.)  The implementation
       involves the use of a raw nneettlliinnkk(7) socket and creates a new thread
       for each notification that is delivered to the process.

